  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The statement &quot;It contains a banana bond&quot; is incorrect about Borazine.</p><p>Borazine, also known as inorganic benzene or borazole, is a chemical compound with the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></math>. Borazine is a hexagonal planar molecule with alternating boron and nitrogen atoms, and it exhibits some structural and chemical similarities to benzene.&nbsp;Borazine is an aromatic compound with electron&nbsp;delocalization. It does not contain banana bond.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e48a0b6a-7428-4678-89fb-852a06f32df8-9928474.PNG\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 335px;\" /></p><p>On heating, borazine hydrolyses slowly.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>BO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
